/bin/
/dist/
*.wav
*.test
coverage.out

# Soak output (scripts/soak.sh). Kept out of the tree on purpose: the logs are
# evidence for one run on one machine, and CI retains its own as artefacts.
/soak-logs/

# Mutation output (scripts/mutation-report.sh). Same argument as the soak
# logs: a report is evidence for one run on one commit, and the scheduled
# workflow keeps its own as an artefact. What DOES belong in the tree is the
# triage of a report — docs/mutation.md.
/mutation-out/

# Stray agent worktrees
.claude/
